@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Services}/{GlobalValues.Service_Path_Part_Live_Region}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Service_Name_Live_Region @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Service_Name_Live_Region @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</h1>


<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> The Live Region Service is part of the required BlazorRamp.Core package.
</p>

<p>
    The installation of this Core package along with the Live Region Service is detailed on the
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Getting_Started}{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">@GlobalValues.Getting_Started_Name - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</a>
    page.
</p>

<p>
    Below is the release history for the BlazorRamp.Core package which contains the Live Region Service.
</p>


<h2 id="release-history">Release history</h2>

<ol reversed class="history-list">
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.1.4 — <time datetime="2026-08-21">August 21, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Added CSS variables for border radius groupings.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.1.2 — <time datetime="2026-08-16">August 16, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Fixed typo in secondary colour variable and bumped default button border colour value from primary 40 to 50.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.1.2 — <time datetime="2026-08-16">August 16, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Fixed typo in secondary colour variable and bumped default button border colour value from primary 40 to 50.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.1.1 — <time datetime="2026-06-10">June 11, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Restored binary compatibility for pre-compiled consumers by adding an explicit single-parameter overload of MakeAnnouncement. 
                The v1.1.0 release introduced a replayable parameter with a default value which, while source-compatible, broke binary compatibility 
                for assemblies compiled against the previous interface signature.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.1.0 — <time datetime="2026-06-10">June 10, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Enabled the replayable flag in the live region service so when making an announcement
                you can choose not to have the announcement added to the announcement history.
                Defaults to true.

            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.8 — <time datetime="2026-04-12">April 12, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Forced JS module to load early for global server and global auto.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.7 — <time datetime="2026-02-28">February 28, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Change to how the CSS resolves the included Roboto font file to avoid issues if including polyfills such as oddbird's css anchor positioning polyfill.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.6 — <time datetime="2026-02-14">February 14, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Change to the script file to stop an edge case issue with the modal dialog framework that did not toggle the open state of the announcement history dialog correctly.
                Just made the previous patch more robust.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.5 — <time datetime="2026-02-13">February 13, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Amended the Core script file to stop an edge case issue with the modal dialog framework that did not toggle the open state of the announcement history dialog correctly.
                This meant clicking twice on the alert button to open it
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.4 — <time datetime="2026-02-10">February 10, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Updated the script file so it that works with nested dialogs in preparation for the modal dialog framework. On the close of a dialog if there is another still
                open the announcement dialog and live regions will move to it.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.3 — <time datetime="2026-02-05">February 05, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Added an additional css variable to the core package required by the switch, and amended two
                unused variable values.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.2 — <time datetime="2026-02-01">February 02, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Resolved JSDisconnectedException in the live region service disposal that could appear when debugging
                when quickly switching between server and wasm
            </li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.1 — <time datetime="2026-02-01">February 01, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Added additional target support for <span class="code-span">..NET 9.0 & .NET 10.0</span></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h3>
            Version 1.0.0 — <time datetime="2026-01-25">January 25, 2026</time>
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Initial release part of the <span class="code-span">BlazorRamp.Core v1.0.0</span> NuGet package, only targeting <span class="code-span">.NET 8.0</span></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ol>



